tection, context cancellation checks, empty key/negative revision validation, and revision-conflict detection plus deep copy on Snapshot inside storage.go, while api.go, export.go, and replica.go just wrap their calls with context.Background() internally.\n\nFor Put's expected-revision logic, I'm working out that a brand-new key should expect revision 0.\n\nI'm reasoning through the compare-and-swap semantics: if the key doesn't exist, expected must be 0; if it exists, the stored revision must match expected exactly, otherwise it's a conflict -- confirming this against how TestCAS exercises sequential Puts.\n\nNow I'm writing the Go storage package with a mutex-protected map and defined error sentinels for conflicts, empty keys, negative revisions, and canceled contexts...\n\nStill writing Put logic...\n\nStill writing module files...\n\nI'm double-checking the concurrent test logic: twenty goroutines race to put the same key, only one wins the lock and bumps the revision to 1, the rest hit conflict errors as expected. The behavior checks out, so I'll proceed to write the files.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":16687,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":435},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b9723f9-dfe3-4e61-98aa-6dd5203c0d18","uuid":"ba603c11-c9fe-47e7-962c-b1a75bd13838"}
